Business continuity planning ensures that critical business functions can continue or recover within acceptable timeframes when unexpected disruptions occur. Azure provides capabilities that can form part of a broader organizational business continuity strategy.

A business continuity plan may include:

* Critical workload identification
* RTO and RPO definitions
* Backup
* Disaster recovery
* Redundant infrastructure
* Monitoring
* Communication procedures
* Recovery testing
* Documented runbooks

For example, an online banking organization can identify payment processing as a critical service and design redundant infrastructure, backup, monitoring, and disaster recovery procedures around its required recovery objectives.

A real-life use case is a company maintaining operations during a datacenter outage, cyber incident, hardware failure, or other major disruption.

Business continuity is broader than disaster recovery: disaster recovery is one component of the overall strategy, while business continuity considers people, processes, technology, communication, and recovery requirements together.
